(7207202, 1109424, 108580, '<td valign="top">I gave it a 6 btw Anita. I don''t believe punishing someone for their interpretation of processing. And for me a 5 (or less) is punishment. What did the colour shot look like? Possibly a 7 in Colour where 90% of the shot would have been black or grey and just the red bill standing out. Black and white in Wildlife is used for more dramatic and emotive work.</td>', 'I gave it a 6 btw Anita. I don''t believe punishing someone for their interpretation of processing. And for me a 5 (or less) is punishment. What did the colour shot look like? Possibly a 7 in Colour where 90% of the shot would have been black or grey and just the red bill standing out. Black and white in Wildlife is used for more dramatic and emotive work.', '2014-04-23 04:23:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7207206, 1109424, 108580, '<td valign="top">I''ve just noticed that Avg (commenters): 5.0000! That means the other two commenters gave you a any one of these combinations 5 and a 4, 6 and a 3, 7 and 2 or 8 and a 1 (With my 6 equals an average of 5...)</td>', 'I''ve just noticed that Avg (commenters): 5.0000! That means the other two commenters gave you a any one of these combinations 5 and a 4, 6 and a 3, 7 and 2 or 8 and a 1 (With my 6 equals an average of 5...)', '2014-04-23 04:27:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7207210, 1108895, 142425, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by HarveyG:</b></div><hr/><i> Not fond of ... or hand of man (man made object) in a "Wildlife" challenge. Wildlife photography avoids these things, and presents wildlife without it ...</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually, this statement couldn''t be more wrong. Check out the British Wildlife Photography Awards where there are plenty of examples of manmade objects interacting with modern wildlife, and even a dedicated category for "Urban Wildlife". By definition it is the ''life'' that is wild regardless of the static background it chooses to be wild among.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2014-04-23 03:49:45.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by HarveyG: Not fond of ... or hand of man (man made object) in a "Wildlife" challenge. Wildlife photography avoids these things, and presents wildlife without it ...  Actually, this statement couldn''t be more wrong. Check out the British Wildlife Photography Awards where there are plenty of examples of manmade objects interacting with modern wildlife, and even a dedicated category for "Urban Wildlife". By definition it is the ''life'' that is wild regardless of the static background it chooses to be wild among.', '2014-04-23 04:44:12.000000', '2014-04-23 04:49:45.000000', 0),
